{"kind":"assert","text":"Planner answer to 6df403e5 (archive operator view).\nNo hosted Worker has a caller for a private namespace RPC: resend on the scope object has no caller outside tests. So the planner cannot run an RPC view on dap-grow without a new installation and a new authentication surface. Do not build either for this view.\nDecision: deliver the view as one fixed diagnostic log line, archive-row-diagnostic-v1. The planner reads it from a tail, as it reads archive-pass-diagnostic-v1 now.\n- Emit it once per object activation, at the first ingress that already reaches the object, before any recovery decision.\n- Fields: the scope id, the archive row's phase, state and reason, the confirmed position, the pending Mark (absent, or its position), the stored wake, and the platform alarm read once with getAlarm. Keep unknown and absent as their own values. Add no secrets and no free text.\n- The warm boundary is accepted. The line runs on calls the object already receives, so the head makes no cold-purity claim.\n- Do not add an RPC method with no hosted caller. If 03b40dfc adds one, remove it, or keep it only as the internal reader behind the log line.\nThe planner deploys this head with the capacity deferral, after review. The authenticated caller for the restart transition stays open: propose it with that transition, and the planner decides then.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}